From 5c5ca31197774b8356f45140465f6c7982b37b92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:29:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] Safarium: add Safari's tab right-click menu

Right-click or Control-click a tab, the current tab's address field, a
vertical sidebar tab or a Tab Overview card for Reload, Duplicate,
Pin/Unpin, Mute/Unmute, Move Tab to New Window, Close Tab, Close Other
Tabs, Close Tabs to the Right (Below), Copy Link and Arrange Tabs By
Title or Website. The commands run through TabStripModel's own tab
context menu commands; mute is per tab, as in Safari.

AppKit answers clicks in the toolbar with its Customize Toolbar menu
before item views see them, so the tab bar watches its window's right
and Control clicks. The bar now also refreshes when only a tab's pinned
state changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
